StreamCleanup
Automatic memory & cache cleaner for Windows 11 streaming machines. Built for setups running Tape Surf + NinjaTrader + OBS together.

Setup (one time only)

Copy StreamCleanup.ps1 to anywhere on the remote machine
Right-click the file → Run as Administrator
It installs itself as a Windows scheduled task and closes
Done — it will now run automatically in the background every 45 minutes


What it cleans
TargetDetailsWindows Temp folders%TEMP%, %TMP%, C:\Windows\TempOpera browser cacheClears accumulated cache from the OBS browser sessionWindows PrefetchSafe to clear, Windows rebuilds it automaticallyDNS cacheFlushed via ipconfig /flushdnsDelivery Optimisation cacheWindows Update background cacheRecycle BinEmptied silentlyStandby memoryFlushes RAM held by idle background processes
What it will NOT touch

Tape Surf
NinjaTrader / Ninja
OBS / obs64
Opera (the running process itself — only its cache folder)


Changing the interval
Open StreamCleanup.ps1 in Notepad and change this line near the top:
$IntervalMinutes = 45
Then uninstall the old task (see below) and re-run the script as Administrator to reinstall with the new interval.

Logs
Every run writes to StreamCleanup.log in the same folder as the script. Check this to see how much memory is being freed each cycle.

Uninstalling
Open PowerShell as Administrator and run:
powershellUnregister-ScheduledTask -TaskName "StreamMemoryCleanup" -Confirm:$false

Requirements

Windows 11
PowerShell 5.1+ (built into Windows 11)
Must be run as Administrator on first install only
